    "days": [
      {
        "day_number": 1,
        "title": "January 1",
        "content": "<p>Morning</p>\n<p><em>“They did eat of the fruit of the land of Canaan that year.”</em></p>\n<p>Joshua 5:12</p>\n<p><strong>Editorial morning reflection:</strong> Faith is not denial of evidence, pain, or honest questions. It is a growing reliance on God's character that can seek wisdom, receive help, and take the next faithful step without pretending certainty we do not have.</p>\n<p><strong>Practice:</strong> Read the verse once more before the day gathers pace. Name one concrete way its truth can shape your attention, speech, or action today.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Trustworthy God, hold me amid uncertainty and guide my next step in wisdom, courage, and love. Amen.</p>\n<p>Evening</p>\n<p><em>“We will be glad and rejoice in you.”</em></p>\n<p>Song of Solomon 1:4</p>\n<p><strong>Editorial evening reflection:</strong> Worship turns attention toward the triune God and reorders desire around truth, beauty, justice, and love. Praise need not hide grief; thanksgiving and lament can both be faithful speech before God.</p>\n<p><strong>Practice:</strong> Read the verse once more and review the day without denial or self-contempt. Give thanks, name what needs repair, and entrust tomorrow to God.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Father, Son, and Holy Spirit, receive my worship and make my whole life an offering of gratitude, truth, and love. Amen.</p>",
        "references": [
          "Joshua 5:12",
          "Song of Solomon 1:4"
        ]
      },
      {
        "day_number": 2,
        "title": "January 2",
        "content": "<p>Morning</p>\n<p><em>“Continue in prayer.”</em></p>\n<p>Colossians 4:2</p>\n<p><strong>Editorial morning reflection:</strong> Prayer brings our real lives before God: gratitude and need, confidence and uncertainty, confession and lament. Speak honestly, listen patiently, and remain open to help that may arrive through other people.</p>\n<p><strong>Practice:</strong> Read the verse once more before the day gathers pace. Name one concrete way its truth can shape your attention, speech, or action today.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Faithful God, receive my honest prayer, deepen my trust, and help me recognize the answer I need rather than only the answer I expect. Amen.</p>\n<p>Evening</p>\n<p><em>“Let the people renew their strength.”</em></p>\n<p>Isaiah 41:1</p>\n<p><strong>Editorial evening reflection:</strong> Biblical hope is patient confidence in God's faithfulness, not a promise that every difficulty will quickly disappear. Let hope make room for honest lament and sustain one concrete act of love today.</p>\n<p><strong>Practice:</strong> Read the verse once more and review the day without denial or self-contempt. Give thanks, name what needs repair, and entrust tomorrow to God.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> God of hope, keep me faithful while I wait and let your promised future strengthen love in the present. Amen.</p>",
        "references": [
