        "day_number": 66,
        "title": "March 6",
        "content": "<p>Morning</p>\n<p><em>“You must be born again.”</em></p>\n<p>John 3:7</p>\n<p><strong>Editorial morning reflection:</strong> This verse directs our attention to Jesus Christ, the eternal Son who became truly human for our salvation. Receive what it reveals about his character or work, and let trust in him take visible form in love.</p>\n<p><strong>Practice:</strong> Read the verse once more before the day gathers pace. Name one concrete way its truth can shape your attention, speech, or action today.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Lord Jesus Christ, true God and true human, draw me into your life and teach me to follow you in love. Amen.</p>\n<p>Evening</p>\n<p><em>“Before destruction the heart of man is haughty.”</em></p>\n<p>Proverbs 18:12</p>\n<p><strong>Editorial evening reflection:</strong> Christ will come again to judge the living and the dead, so our choices matter. The warning calls us to humble repentance and faithful love, not speculation about another person's fate or pressure built from panic.</p>\n<p><strong>Practice:</strong> Read the verse once more and review the day without denial or self-contempt. Give thanks, name what needs repair, and entrust tomorrow to God.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Righteous and merciful Christ, keep me watchful, humble, and active in love as I await your kingdom. Amen.</p>",
        "references": [
