        "day_number": 83,
        "title": "March 23",
        "content": "<p>Morning</p>\n<p><em>“His sweat was as it were great drops of blood falling down to the ground.”</em></p>\n<p>Luke 22:44</p>\n<p><strong>Editorial morning reflection:</strong> The cross reveals Christ's self-giving love and God's refusal to abandon a wounded world. Receive forgiveness as grace, name harm truthfully, and let reconciliation include accountability and repair.</p>\n<p><strong>Practice:</strong> Read the verse once more before the day gathers pace. Name one concrete way its truth can shape your attention, speech, or action today.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Crucified and risen Lord, forgive me, free me from sin, and make your self-giving love visible in my life. Amen.</p>\n<p>Evening</p>\n<p><em>“I tell you that, if these should hold their peace, the stones would immediately cry out.”</em></p>\n<p>Luke 19:40</p>\n<p><strong>Editorial evening reflection:</strong> God's peace is more than avoidance of conflict. It grows through truth, justice, reconciliation, wise boundaries, and protection for people at risk. Seek peace without asking the harmed to carry its whole cost.</p>\n<p><strong>Practice:</strong> Read the verse once more and review the day without denial or self-contempt. Give thanks, name what needs repair, and entrust tomorrow to God.</p>\n<p><strong>Prayer:</strong> Prince of Peace, make me truthful and courageous in reconciliation, and lead me in ways that protect dignity and life. Amen.</p>",
        "references": [
          "Luke 22:44",
          "Luke 19:40"
        ]
      },
